{
  "claim": "C-030",
  "text": "On the runs of C-029, a reviewer from another model family agreed with the Nemotron reviewer on at least 95% of the changes both reviewed, and Nemotron 3.5 Lightning ran the summarize steps with no more cut-off calls than Ultra, for under a tenth of its dollars per call.",
  "scope": "The ladder's task runs of C-029. Ultra reviews each change after the gates pass and `gpt-oss-120b` gives a second opinion on the same change. Every reviewed change had passed the project's tests, so the agreement is on changes that pass their tests; no failing change was put to both reviewers. Where they disagreed, Ultra blocked a change that passed its tests and the second reviewer approved it. The small tier's steps are compared with Ultra alone's steps of the same type on the same tasks: the share of tool calls that returned an error, the share of calls cut off at the output limit, and dollars per call. The claim names summarize steps only. On navigate steps Lightning's tool calls returned errors more often than Ultra's (it guessed absolute paths and corrected them after the tool's message), and Ultra ran too few read steps to compare; the evidence reports both, and Lightning alone on the same suites, none of which is claimed.",
